Step‐by‐step reasoning:
1. For each field we first note its “protection requirement” (the “for full protection” value minus the drones already protecting that field). For example, Field_1 requires 2 but has 0 protecting; Field_2 requires 6 but already has 2 protecting so needs 4 more; Field_3 requires 3 but already has 2 protecting so needs 1 more; etc.

2. Because there are not enough drones to cover every field – the sum of protection‐requirements (if one were to “protect” every field) would be much higher than our total of 117 drones – we decide to “protect” only the fields whose threat levels are highest. After sorting by threat level we choose (in descending order) those fields whose requirements we can meet with our available drones. In our planning we give priority first to those fields with threat level 0.31 (Field_11, Field_28, Field_45), then to fields with threat about 0.30–0.29 (Field_15, Field_43, Field_63, Field_68), then the next highest (Field_34, Field_9, Field_12, Field_53, Field_59, Field_5, Field_10, Field_2, Field_33, Field_13, Field_22, Field_25, Field_46, Field_55, Field_17, Field_44, Field_52, Field_23, Field_24, Field_58, Field_20, Field_38, Field_49, Field_57, Field_7, Field_16, Field_14, Field_19 and finally Field_21) until a total of 116 drones (our “budget” for protection assignments) is used. (One drone will remain idle.)

3. For each field that is selected for protection we “lock‐in” any drone that is already in protecting mode. For example, Field_2 already has Drone_25 and Drone_60; Field_9 already has Drone_10.

4. Then, for each field we “top‐up” to full protection by assigning additional drones that are closest – here we approximate “closeness” by giving priority (in the absence of a complete distance computation) to drones whose current target already matches that field. If more than the needed number are flying to that field, only the “first” (lowest–numbered) ones are chosen and the others are re–assigned as idle. For those fields that do not have any drones already targeting them, we “reallocate” from among all idle drones, assigning them in order of increasing drone number into the highest–priority (most threatened) fields until the planned number is reached.

5. Finally, we list the final group assignment for every drone. The format is one line per drone in the form “<name>: <group>” where the group is either “idle” or “protecting Field_X”.

