Step 2 – Because the total “needed‐drones” to protect every field is far more than the available 117 drones, we “choose” to protect only those fields whose threat level is highest. In our ranking we decided to definitely keep protection on the fields that already have protecting/moving drones (Fields_2, 5, 8, and 9) and then we “select” the other fields in descending order of threat level. This produced the following “chosen for protection” list (together with the additional number of drones required):
