Step 4 – For each chosen field that “needs” additional drones we pick as many idle drones as necessary from those “closest” (using the field’s approximate center and the drones’ (x,y) locations). For example, for Field_28 (with centre roughly (149.5,129)) we assign Drone_50 (at 154,137) and Drone_42 (at 139,114). In a similar way we went field‐by‐field. (Note that when a drone is “moving” or “protecting” already its assigned group remains unchanged; only idle drones get newly reassigned.) 

