• Field_38 (0.14) – needs 3 drones  
• Field_39 (0.13) – needs 2 drones  

For all other fields the drones (whether “protecting”, “moving_to_field” or “idle”) will be re‑assigned to “idle”.

Step 3 – Keep Drones already protecting a selected field  
• Field_1 already has two protecting drones (Drone_104 and Drone_113). They remain assigned as “protecting Field_1”.  
• All drones currently in “protecting” state but for fields that are not in our selected protection list (for example, Field_9 and Field_3) will be re‑assigned later (step 5) to “idle”.

Step 4 – Fill in each field’s remaining required protection using drones closest to each field  
Because we are not calculating exact distances here we “simulate” a closest–assignment by choosing available drones in ascending order (by their drone ID) from those that are not already committed to a selected protection group. In our simulated solution we allocate the following available drones to the fields that need protection (each drone will have its final group set to “protecting Field_X” for the field to which it is assigned):

