──────────────────────────── Step 2. Decide which fields “need” active protection based on threat levels

Because available drones are limited and our goal is to “minimize damage,” we choose to protect only those fields whose “bird‐threat level” is highest. (In our plan we decide to only “protect” fields with threat levels roughly 0.07 or higher. Fields with very low threat like Field_1, Field_2, Field_3, Field_4, Field_5, Field_6, Field_9, Field_16, etc. are not “worth” having drones over them once they’ve been sent—even if drones are already “in the air”.) 

